 have:\n\\[ PX \\cdot PB = 25 \\cdot (AB + AC - 20), \\]\nwhere \\(25\\) is the length of \\(PQ\\).\n\nSimilarly, for point \\(Q\\), we have:\n\\[ QX \\cdot QA = 25 \\cdot (AB + AC - 15). \\]\n\nSince \\(PX \\cdot PB = PY \\cdot PC\\), we can use the fact that the power of point \\(P\\) with respect to the circumcircle is the same for \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[ AB \\cdot AC = 25 \\cdot 15 = 375. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(AB \\cdot AC\\) is \\(375\\), and the sum \\(m+n\\) is:\n\\[ m+n = 375 + 1 = 376. \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{376}\n\\]",
